# DanNet SHACL shapes: INFERRED model only.
#
# Relation-completeness checks that hold only after OWL inference has supplied
# the missing direction of inverse relations (e.g. `ontolex:isLexicalizedSenseOf`
# from the asserted `ontolex:lexicalizedSense`).
#
# IMPORTANT: never run these against the BASE (asserted) graph; doing so
# produces ~77k false positives (see base.ttl). These shapes are combined with
# base.ttl and validated against the inference model via the opt-in
# `validate-inferred-db`.
#
# NOTE: property shapes are deliberately given explicit IRIs (rather than the
# usual blank nodes) so that validation reports can group violations by a
# stable shape identity.

@prefix sh:      <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix ontolex: <http://www.w3.org/ns/lemon/ontolex#> .
@prefix dns:     <https://wordnet.dk/dannet/schema/> .

## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## LexicalSense (dn:): every sense lexicalizes exactly one synset.
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dns:SenseSynsetShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    ## dns:DanNetSenseTarget is defined in base.ttl, which is always loaded
    ## together with this file (see `inferred-shapes` in shapes.clj).
    sh:target dns:DanNetSenseTarget ;
    sh:property dns:SenseSynsetShape-isLexicalizedSenseOf .

dns:SenseSynsetShape-isLexicalizedSenseOf a sh:PropertyShape ;
    sh:path ontolex:isLexicalizedSenseOf ;
    sh:minCount 1 ;
    sh:maxCount 1 ;
    sh:class ontolex:LexicalConcept ;
    sh:severity sh:Violation ;
    sh:message "A sense must lexicalize exactly one synset." .
